      "parent_visual": {
        "decision": "Hold for explicit artistic decision on whether generic-blossom readability and weaker petal/lip separation adequately convey the orchid theme relative to marketing. This is fidelity uncertainty, not a proven mechanical defect or authority to edit art.",
        "hardware": "Chunky faceted long clasp and conspicuous backing/corner joints; dark jade seam/stepped rim can look slightly lifted. Open latch separation is expected, and no broken hinge is established at screenshot scale.",
        "limitations": "Frozen still-image review only; supplied technical passes were not rerun. No final user approval, photoreal equivalence, physical-phone performance, cultural authentication or continuous mechanical certification. Open disengaged latch is expected; hidden exterior lid ornament in open views is not missing. Brief requires differentiated orchid anatomy but explicitly permits stylized enamel, not botanical reconstruction. Source README already acknowledges generic mobile blossoms, repetitive arrangement, chunky hardware and slightly lifted-looking seam. Do not erase those limits because technical flower counts pass.",
        "quality": "Complete coherent celadon/brass chest with three pink/ivory flowers and gold frame; open cavity and silhouette fit both viewports. Substantial uncertainty remains in the theme-defining floral specificity rather than any demonstrated runtime defect.",
        "terrain": "Not terrain: three shallow floral appliques with stems/leaves. Actual desktop flowers can read as generic broad-lobed blossoms; pale petals lose separation on mobile. Marketing shows clearer layered/cupped petals, magenta lips and amber throats than the actual whole-object captures resolve.",
        "texture": "Actual celadon reads as cloudy/streaky coloration rather than depthful ceramic glaze; broad smooth enamel lobes and simplified leaves remain visible. Marketing is satin and clouded too, so gloss alone is not the hold."
      },
